1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,920
On the evening of Saturday, 7 September 1996,
Tupac Shakur took a front-row seat at the

2
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:21,020
MGM Grand in Las Vegas, to watch
Mike Tyson fight Bruce Seldon.

3
00:00:21,651 --> 00:00:25,356
He was twenty-five years old, and one
of the most famous rappers in the world.

4
00:00:25,988 --> 00:00:27,713
Six days later, he would be dead.

5
00:00:28,313 --> 00:00:33,453
This is the documented story of that night, and
of the long search for the people responsible.

6
00:00:42,495 --> 00:00:46,020
Tupac was born in East
Harlem, New York, in 1971.

7
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:50,400
By 1996 he was a recording
star, a film actor,

8
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,540
and a man who was rarely out of the news.

9
00:00:53,183 --> 00:00:57,903
In October 1995, Marion Suge Knight,
the head of Death Row Records,

10
00:00:58,303 --> 00:01:00,663
posted a bond of one point
four million dollars,

11
00:01:01,003 --> 00:01:03,883
and Tupac signed with his label
while he appealed a conviction.

12
00:01:04,561 --> 00:01:10,721
In February 1996 he released All Eyez on Me, a
double album that produced two number one singles.

13
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:15,925
Three days before the fight, he had walked
into Radio City Music Hall for the MTV Video

14
00:01:15,925 --> 00:01:16,685
Music Awards.

15
00:01:17,445 --> 00:01:20,170
Now he was in Las Vegas with
Knight and a group of friends,

16
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:22,270
including his fiancee, Kidada Jones.

17
00:01:33,733 --> 00:01:35,753
The fight lasted less than two minutes.

18
00:01:36,333 --> 00:01:37,993
Tyson won by a first round knockout.

19
00:01:38,595 --> 00:01:42,500
Afterwards, Tupac embraced Tyson,
his friend, just off the arena floor.

20
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:46,685
Minutes later, in the hotel and
casino area outside the arena,

21
00:01:47,185 --> 00:01:50,525
Tupac, Knight and their group got into
a fight with another group of men.

22
00:01:51,106 --> 00:01:56,326
Hotel surveillance video showed Tupac and Knight
hitting a young man named Orlando Anderson,

23
00:01:56,706 --> 00:01:57,886
near a bank of elevators.

24
00:01:58,523 --> 00:02:01,783
Police say Anderson belonged to
the South Side Compton Crips,

25
00:02:02,203 --> 00:02:05,323
and that his uncle, Duane
Davis, known as Keffe D,

26
00:02:05,603 --> 00:02:06,903
was in the group with him.

27
00:02:07,424 --> 00:02:10,574
Hotel security broke it
up, and Tupac's group left.

28
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:19,820
Over the next two hours, they
stopped at a hotel and at a house,

29
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:23,120
and then set out for a
nightclub called Club 662.

30
00:02:23,813 --> 00:02:27,638
Knight was driving a black BMW,
with Tupac in the passenger seat,

31
00:02:27,818 --> 00:02:29,398
and friends followed in other cars.

32
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:34,913
Around eleven, police on bicycles stopped
them for loud music and license plates that

33
00:02:34,913 --> 00:02:38,293
were not properly displayed, and
let them go without a ticket.

34
00:02:38,879 --> 00:02:41,279
A few minutes later, at
about quarter past eleven,

35
00:02:41,919 --> 00:02:46,139
the BMW stopped at a red light,
at Flamingo Road and Koval Lane,

36
00:02:46,719 --> 00:02:47,799
just east of the Strip.

37
00:02:48,383 --> 00:02:52,808
A white Cadillac pulled up beside it, and someone
in the back seat opened fire into the BMW.

38
00:03:04,562 --> 00:03:06,167
Tupac was hit several times.

39
00:03:06,907 --> 00:03:08,067
Knight was hurt by a fragment.

40
00:03:08,654 --> 00:03:12,919
Knight drove on for about a mile, until
police on bicycles stopped the car again,

41
00:03:13,079 --> 00:03:14,039
near Harmon Avenue.

42
00:03:14,558 --> 00:03:17,403
Paramedics took both men to
University Medical Center,

43
00:03:17,643 --> 00:03:19,403
and surgeons operated on Tupac.

44
00:03:19,903 --> 00:03:21,143
He was kept on life support.

45
00:03:21,667 --> 00:03:25,567
He died on Friday, 13 September
1996, in the afternoon.

46
00:03:26,207 --> 00:03:27,172
He was twenty-five.

47
00:03:37,833 --> 00:03:42,753
His records kept selling, and in 2017 he
was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of

48
00:03:42,753 --> 00:03:44,773
Fame, in his first year of eligibility.

49
00:04:02,528 --> 00:04:04,753
Las Vegas police opened
a murder investigation,

50
00:04:05,093 --> 00:04:05,793
but it stalled.

51
00:04:06,377 --> 00:04:10,562
Police said that few new clues came
in, and that witnesses would not talk.

52
00:04:19,895 --> 00:04:24,380
In October 1996, police in Compton
searched homes connected to the case,

53
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:26,180
but no charge came from it.

54
00:04:26,611 --> 00:04:29,371
A year later, the homicide
sergeant leading the case,

55
00:04:29,731 --> 00:04:34,111
Kevin Manning, told the Las Vegas Sun that
the investigation was at a standstill.

56
00:04:34,643 --> 00:04:39,348
Anderson, the man beaten in the hotel, was
questioned by police in Compton and in Las

57
00:04:39,348 --> 00:04:43,488
Vegas, and released. Through his
lawyer, he denied any involvement.

58
00:04:44,288 --> 00:04:48,108
He was never charged, and in 1998 he
was killed in a separate shooting.

59
00:04:48,647 --> 00:04:51,487
The gun was never found, and
neither was the Cadillac.

60
00:04:52,103 --> 00:04:54,188
Over the years, many theories spread.

61
00:04:54,908 --> 00:04:58,948
This film sticks to what police, prosecutors
and the courts have put on the record.

62
00:04:59,539 --> 00:05:02,539
And one man who says he was
in that Cadillac kept talking.

63
00:05:03,045 --> 00:05:06,305
Duane Davis described the
night to investigators in 2008,

64
00:05:06,825 --> 00:05:10,885
to a television series in
2018, and in a memoir in 2019,

65
00:05:11,265 --> 00:05:12,445
called Compton Street Legend.

66
00:05:13,147 --> 00:05:17,292
He wrote that he was in the Cadillac, and
that someone else in the car fired the shots.

67
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:20,840
For years he spoke openly,
and no charge followed.

68
00:05:29,428 --> 00:05:34,333
In June 2023, Tupac received a
star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.

69
00:05:47,995 --> 00:05:51,220
The next month, Las Vegas police
searched a house in Henderson,

70
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:55,780
Nevada, and took away computers, a
phone, and a copy of Davis's book.

71
00:05:56,386 --> 00:06:01,511
On 29 September 2023, Davis
was arrested near his home.

72
00:06:02,451 --> 00:06:04,751
Police described him as
the last living suspect.

73
00:06:20,433 --> 00:06:23,393
He was indicted on one count of
open murder with a deadly weapon,

74
00:06:23,633 --> 00:06:27,753
with a gang enhancement. In November
2023, he pleaded not guilty.

75
00:06:28,402 --> 00:06:30,927
Prosecutors said they would
not seek the death penalty.

76
00:06:31,667 --> 00:06:35,767
Davis was held in jail while he waited,
and the trial date was moved several times.

77
00:06:45,528 --> 00:06:48,013
Prosecutors did not say
that Davis fired the gun.

78
00:06:48,533 --> 00:06:52,193
They said he was the shot caller, who got
the weapon and handed it to the gunman,

79
00:06:52,513 --> 00:06:54,133
in revenge for the hotel fight.

80
00:06:54,663 --> 00:06:58,248
They said the gunman was either Anderson,
or another man in the back seat.

81
00:06:59,308 --> 00:07:01,568
Police say the other men
in the car have since died.

82
00:07:02,156 --> 00:07:07,056
The trial began in August 2026, and
jurors heard nine days of testimony.

83
00:07:07,708 --> 00:07:10,818
Prosecutors leaned on Davis's
own words, in his book,

84
00:07:11,138 --> 00:07:13,158
in his interviews, and
in what he told police.

85
00:07:13,899 --> 00:07:16,584
The defense said he had
exaggerated his stories for money,

86
00:07:17,024 --> 00:07:19,524
that the gun and the Cadillac
were never recovered,

87
00:07:20,024 --> 00:07:21,864
and that prosecutors had waited too long.

88
00:07:22,405 --> 00:07:29,225
On 31 August 2026, in under three hours,
the jury found Davis guilty of first degree

89
00:07:29,225 --> 00:07:30,505
murder with a deadly weapon.

90
00:07:31,108 --> 00:07:35,988
On 13 October, Judge Carli Kierny sentenced
him to forty years to life in prison.

91
00:07:36,748 --> 00:07:40,408
Tupac's siblings, Mopreme and
Sekyiwa Shakur, spoke at the hearing.

92
00:07:41,064 --> 00:07:45,864
Davis said he would appeal, and a notice of
appeal to the Nevada Supreme Court was filed

93
00:07:45,864 --> 00:07:48,804
on 30 October. That appeal is pending.

94
00:07:49,501 --> 00:07:54,276
So the official record now says that a
jury held Davis responsible for the murder.

95
00:07:55,176 --> 00:07:57,756
Prosecutors said he supplied
the gun and ordered the attack.

96
00:07:58,476 --> 00:08:00,056
They did not argue that he fired it.

97
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:04,420
Thirty years, one verdict, and
no one convicted as the shooter.

98
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:06,220
Is this case closed?
